From: minimal vendored-patch series <patches@minimal.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] stdio_client: harden the read loop, ping and stop path

minimal-mcp patch. Four hardening fixes to the stdio transport, all in the
same file:

- The read loop caps the unterminated-line buffer (16 MiB) in both platform
  branches. A child that never emits a newline -- misbehaving or hostile --
  previously grew data_buffer without bound, an OOM at the hands of the
  server process. Overflow breaks out to the fail-all-pending block the
  closed-pipe path already uses.

- Response matching requires the message to have no "method" field. A
  server-originated REQUEST carries a non-null id too; matching on id alone
  let such a request consume a pending client request with a colliding id,
  answering its waiter with an empty success.

- ping() reports liveness on any RESULT. The spec's ping answers with an
  empty object, so the original `result.empty()` check declared healthy
  servers that echo richer ping state dead.

- stop_server_process probes with waitpid(WNOHANG) BEFORE signalling. An
  already-exited and reaped child answers ECHILD, and its pid may by then
  have been recycled: kill() would signal an innocent process. Only a
  "still running" probe result earns the SIGTERM/SIGKILL ladder.

Applies after cpp-mcp-stop-server-race.patch (this file sorts after it; the
stop-path hunk's context is that patch's output).

---
 src/mcp_stdio_client.cpp | 121 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 99 insertions(+), 22 deletions(-)

